<title>USA: Norfolk says 53 pct shrs defeat measure.</title>
<headline>Norfolk says 53 pct shrs defeat measure.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norfolk Southern Corp chief executive officer David Goode said at least 53 percent of Conrail Inc's outstanding shares were voted against a measure that is crucial to Conrail's planner merger with CSX Corp.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference after a special Conrail shareholders meeting, Goode said the figure indicates shareholders &quot;overwhelmingly&quot; defeated the measure.</p>
<p>Goode said any future talks with Conrail and CSX would have to be based on its offer of $115 per share.</p>
</text>
